<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

  <!--
    Expenses' cross-section surface, carved into its own leaf project because one of its
    consumers is still in Base: HoldedExpenseOutboxJob (Humans.Infrastructure/Jobs), which
    stays there because recurring jobs are named by concrete type in Shell's
    UseHumansRecurringJobs roll-call and there is no discovery seam for them yet
    (design §15.6b). A Contracts/ *folder* inside Humans.Expenses would therefore make Base
    reference a section and cycle (design §15.5b,
    memory/architecture/section-project-cycle-fix.md).

    It holds exactly one interface. Everything else Expenses exposes — IExpenseReportServiceRead,
    ExpenseReportDto, ExpenseReportStatus — has no consumer outside the section once
    IbanAccessHandler moves in with it (design §15 step 6), so it stays internal.

    References Humans.Interfaces only. In particular it must not name IHoldedClient,
    HoldedPurchaseDocumentInput, HoldedAttachmentInput or HoldedTransientException: those are
    the Holded connector's and the connector stays in Base, which is the cycle Finance hit in A2
    (memory/architecture/vendor-connectors-own-sections.md).
  -->

  <ItemGroup>
    <ProjectReference Include="..\..\Humans.Interfaces\Humans.Interfaces.csproj" />
  </ItemGroup>

</Project>
